# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
# Anchored to the repo root. Unanchored, `build/` matches a directory of that
# name at any depth — which silently swallowed `skills/build/` when #537 gave the
# `/build` workflow a skill of its own, so the plugin would have shipped without
# its main lifecycle command and nothing would have said so. The pre-existing
# `!prompts/build/` negation was the same bug already worked around once.
/build/
dist/
.venv
.venv/
venv
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Coverage
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Env / secrets
.env
.env.*

# uv
# uv.lock is committed — it pins the dev toolchain the gate runs on, so a fresh
# checkout resolves the same ruff/mypy/pytest every other checkout did.

# State / artifacts
# `.harness/` moved into the gate-ignore block below at #538: it now holds the
# build's `run.json`, and a consuming repo hydrated by `/harness:init` never
# received this line — leaving the run state untracked *and* unignored, so
# `/build`'s own `git add -A && git write-tree` swept it into the tree identity
# the verdict binds to. That is the failure `.evidence/` is in that block to
# prevent.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Worktrees
# .worktrees/ is where a task is isolated (`worktree-isolation`);
# .claude/worktrees/ is the Claude Code CLI's agent-dispatch root — different
# owner, same hazard. Keep comments on their own lines: git does not treat a
# trailing '#' on a pattern line as a comment.
# harness:gate-ignore:begin
.evidence/
.worktrees/
.claude/worktrees/
.harness/
# harness:gate-ignore:end

# OS
.DS_Store

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/

# Claude Code local
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# .codex/ and .gemini/ are committed like .claude/ in this committed-mode repo.
# Ignore only genuinely per-machine bits if any appear (e.g. an absolute-path hook config).

# Working artifacts a task stages at the worktree root. Not covered by
# `.harness/` above — both land at the root.
#   gate.log   — captured verify-gate output, kept for a review to read
#   /design.md — the design stage's artifact on a complex run
# `design.md` is root-anchored: it is a name worth tracking under docs/ or
# specs/, unlike the distinctive `gate.log`.
gate.log
/design.md

# Visual evidence a build loop renders for review (#434). Captures and their
# manifest land at `.evidence/<TICKET-ID>/` in the run worktree — the one
# documented location, so `/review` can hand the reviewer a directory
# (`skills/build/SKILL.md`). Two failure directions, same rule: untracked, each
# capture reads as a dirty worktree to any gate that counts untracked files;
# swept up, `/build`'s `git add -A` in *Independent review* and in *Ship*
# publishes binary captures of seeded state into permanent history of a public
# repo. The pattern lives in the gate-ignore block above with the worktree
# paths that carry the same temp-index hazard.
